  id: Lobes-of-Liver.004
  partName: Lobes of Liver
  descriptionChunks:
  - The liver is a large organ divided into multiple lobes, each contributing to
    essential metabolic functions. It plays a key role in detoxification, protein
    synthesis, and bile production. The liver processes nutrients absorbed from digestion
    and regulates chemical levels in the blood.
  - It also removes toxins and harmful substances, ensuring internal balance. By
    supporting digestion and metabolism, the liver is critical for maintaining overall
    health and enabling proper functioning of other body systems.
